document-difficulty-mode-summary = Automated Security Report
document-meta-garbage-summary = Sanitary Commission Conclusion
paper-neutralized-mode-info =
    ​[bold]THREAT LEVEL ASSESSMENT: NOMINAL[/bold]

    According to automated risk assessment, the current level of anomalous activity in the sector is deemed negligible. All previously contained anomalies have been neutralized, moved, or no longer pose a safety threat.
    ​[bullet] Staffing levels are operating normally.
    ​[bullet] Foundation personnel are instructed to maintain a standard alert level.
    ​[bullet] Routine technical, personnel, and scientific operations are allowed without restrictions.

    ​[italic]Special notice:[/italic] due to the lack of active threats, regional command may initiate large-scale tests, protocol inspections, and unscheduled drills.
paper-safe-mode-info =
    ​[bold]THREAT LEVEL ASSESSMENT: CONTROLLED[/bold]

    The sector contains several anomalous objects classified as Safe. One or more controlled high-risk subjects may be under observation.
    ​[bullet] Foundation staff are permitted unrestricted movement within the sector, except for SCP containment chambers.
    ​[bullet] Presence has been recorded: Safe objects and controlled instances of SCP-035 and/or one Euclid-class object.
    ​[bullet] Threats to personnel are considered unlikely if standard procedures are followed.

    ​[italic]Reminder:[/italic] deviation from approved anomaly handling procedures may lead to localized incidents.
paper-euclid-mode-info =
    ​[bold]THREAT LEVEL ASSESSMENT: ELEVATED[/bold]

    The sector contains active anomalous subjects, including both predictable and unstable instances.
    ​[bullet] Security is advised to closely monitor any interactions with anomalous objects.
    ​[bullet] Presence has been recorded: Safe-class objects, one Euclid, and possibly one Keter-class instance.
    ​[bullet] Situation control requires heightened attention.

    ​[italic]Special notice:[/italic] personnel are instructed to operate within approved procedures, avoid unauthorized contact with anomalies, and immediately report any breaches of containment conditions.
paper-keter-mode-info =
    ​[bold]THREAT LEVEL ASSESSMENT: CRITICAL[/bold]

    The sector has moved to extended containment mode. One or more anomalous subjects present a serious and immediate threat to existing security protocols.
    ​[bullet] Security is required to establish a watch posture at the containment chambers of active SCP objects.
    ​[bullet] Confirmed presence of at least one Keter-class object, as well as possible instances of Euclid and Safe classes.
    ​[bullet] The potential risk of losing control of the objects is high.

    ​[italic]Attention:[/italic] upon receiving a containment breach alert, immediately move to the nearest evacuation zone and await further instructions from regional command.
paper-thaumiel-mode-info =
    ​[bold]THREAT LEVEL ASSESSMENT: UNDETERMINED[/bold]

    The sector contains multiple anomalies simultaneously, classified as objects of elevated control. Their concurrent containment has unpredictable consequences.
    ​[bullet] Security is required to maintain full control over interaction with SCP objects. The number of simultaneous interactions must not exceed one per 20 minutes.
    ​[bullet] Confirmed presence: multiple objects of Keter, Euclid, and Safe classes.
    ​[bullet] The situation is unstable; operations are being conducted under the classification "TOP SECRET".

    ​[italic]Special instruction:[/italic] much of the operation is conducted under restricted clearance. Personnel without the required clearance level are strictly forbidden from intervening.
paper-meta-garbage-successful-info =
    ​[bold]SANITATION COMMISSION CONCLUSION[/bold]

    An unscheduled inspection found:
    ​[bullet] Domestic waste was found on the grounds of the complex (paper cups, food remnants, packaging materials).
    ​[bullet] Pools of technical fluid and unclean residue were recorded in rooms.
    ​[bullet] Lighting: some lamps are broken, and glass fragments have not been removed.
    ​[bullet] The sanitation level has been deemed unsatisfactory.

    ​[italic]Reason:[/italic] the Foundation's resource team was fully tasked with clearing the aftermath of incident ██-███; cleanup was not performed.

    ​[italic]Instruction:[/italic] current staff are ordered to correct the listed violations as soon as possible.
paper-meta-garbage-failed-info =
    ​[bold]SANITATION COMMISSION CONCLUSION[/bold]

    Facility inspection complete. No findings:
    ​[bullet] Floors are dry, and no signs of contamination were found.
    ​[bullet] Lighting is functioning at full capacity.
    ​[bullet] Domestic trash and waste were not detected.

    ​[italic]Finding:[/italic] the sanitation condition of the complex has been deemed satisfactory; no intervention is required.
